{"type":"message","id":"09c36956","parentId":"015a0304","timestamp":"2026-02-11T05:35:28.936Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":" schema shows there's a property `messages.ackReactionScope` that can be set to \"all\" to enable ack reactions on all messages, but that's not quite what the user asked. They want to listen to ALL messages, not just send reactions.\n\nI need to find a setting that controls whether the bot responds to all messages or only when mentioned. For Discord specifically, there might be a setting like `requireMention` or something similar.\n\nLooking at the schema under `channels.discord`, I see properties like:\n- `requireMention` (in the guild-level config)\n- `requireMention` under channel-level `channels.discord.guilds.guildId.channels.channelId`\n- Also there is `groupPolicy`, but that's about allowlist.\n\nSo the key seems to be `requireMention`. When `requireMention` is true, the bot only responds when mentioned. If it's false, it responds to all messages.\n\nAlso, at the agent level, there's `groupChat` configuration under `agents.list[].groupChat` which includes `mentionPatterns`. That's for determining when the bot is mentioned, but not about requiring mention.\n\nWait, the user is asking about listening to all messages \"even without @ing you\". That means they want the bot to be triggered by any message in the channel, not just mentions.\n\nIn Discord, typically bots have a setting in the Discord developer portal for \"Message Content Intent\" and also the bot's code has a setting for whether it requires a mention. In OpenClaw, this is likely controlled by `requireMention` in the channel config.\n\nLet me check the current config: I saw earlier in the config that `channels.discord.guilds` had `\"groupPolicy\": \"allowlist\"`, but I didn't see `requireMention` at the guild level? Actually the config I got earlier showed:\n\n```\n\"channels\": {\n  \"discord\": {\n    \"groupPolicy\": \"allowlist\",\n    \"guilds\": {\n      \"1444592258996244502\": {\n        \"channels\": {\n          \"1471005448948813874\": {}\n        }\n      }\n    },\n    ...\n  }\n}\n```\n\nThere is no `requireMention` set at the guild level or channel level. That likely means it's inheriting the default, which might be true (require mention). The default may be true because it's common for bots to only respond when mentioned.\n\nI need to set `requireMention` to false for this channel (or guild) to listen to all messages. According to the schema, `requireMention` is a boolean field at the guild level and also at the channel level. Setting it at the channel level overrides the guild default.\n\nSo I should patch the config to set `channels.discord.guilds[\"1444592258996244502\"].channels[\"1471005448948813874\"].requireMention = false`.\n\nLet me do that using `gateway config.patch` with a JSON patch. But I need to be careful: The config.patch expects a partial config object that will be merged. So I can construct a patch that updates just that one field.\n\nAlternatively, I could use `gateway config.apply` with the entire modified config, but that's riskier. Let's use config.patch.\n\nThe path for that field is: `channels.discord.guilds.1444592258996244502.channels.1471005448948813874.requireMention`\n\nBut config.patch takes a JSON object with the changes. I'll need to provide the partial structure.\n\nLet me construct a patch object:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"channels\": {\n    \"discord\": {\n      \"guilds\": {\n        \"1444592258996244502\": {\n          \"channels\": {\n            \"1471005448948813874\": {\n              \"requireMention\": false\n            }\n          }\n        }\n      }\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nAnd call gateway config.patch with that raw JSON. However, the config.patch tool expects a `raw` string which is the JSON content. It will merge it into the existing config.\n\nBut wait: The schema shows that `guilds` is an object with property names that are strings (guild IDs). So the patch should be okay.\n\nI need to make sure I don't accidentally overwrite other guild/channel settings. Since it's a deep merge, it should only set that field.\n\nLet's do it.\n</think>\nYes, you can configure me to listen to all messages on this channel without needing an @-mention. The setting is `requireMention` in the Discord channel configuration. Currently it's likely set to `true` (default), which means I only respond when mentioned.\n\nI can patch the config to disable that for this specific channel. Let me do that:That's a config change. I'll patch the OpenClaw config to set `requireMention: false` for this channel:\n\n- Guild ID: `1444592258996244502`\n- Channel ID: `1471005448948813874`"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_9dc63700c9d845a29972ba7b","name":"gateway","arguments":{"action":"config.patch","raw":"{\"channels\":{\"discord\":{\"guilds\":{\"1444592258996244502\":{\"channels\":{\"1471005448948813874\":{\"requireMention\":false}}}}}}"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"stepfun-ai/step-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":91367,"output":1152,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":92519,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770788118218}}
