be it expects a closing brace for something else? Could it be that I need to include the whole config structure? No, patch should merge.\n\nWait, the error is \"invalid end of input at 1:121\". That suggests the parser reached the end of the string at position 121 and expected more. That implies the JSON is incomplete, maybe missing a closing brace. But my counting shows we have enough. Let's double-check the braces:\n\nString: `{\"channels\":{\"discord\":{\"guilds\":{\"1444592258996244502\":{\"channels\":{\"1471005448948813874\":{\"requireMention\":false}}}}}}`\n\nCount opening braces: \n- after first quote: `{` (1)\n- then \"channels\": `{` (2)\n- \"discord\": `{` (3)\n- \"guilds\": `{` (4)\n- \"144459...\": `{` (5)\n- \"channels\": `{` (6)\n- \"147100...\": `{` (7)\n- \"requireMention\": false -> then `}` closes that (7)\n- `}` closes channels (6)\n- `}` closes guild (5)\n- `}` closes guilds (4)\n- `}` closes discord (3)\n- `}` closes channels (2)\n- `}` closes outer (1)\n\nSo we have 7 opening and 7 closing. Good.\n\nMaybe the issue is that the numbers are too large? No.\n\nMaybe the tool expects the JSON to be an object with a specific top-level key like \"config\"? But the example usage in docs: `gateway config.patch --raw '{\"agents\": {\"defaults\": {\"model\": {\"primary\": \"nvidia/stepfun-ai/step-3.5-flash\"}}}}'` shows a simple object. So my patch is in that format.\n\nMaybe the error is unrelated to the JSON content but something else? Could be that the gateway is not running? But I just did config.get successfully.\n\nMaybe the raw string needs to be escaped properly? I'm passing it as a parameter in a tool call, so it's a string. That's fine.\n\nMaybe there's a bug with the config.patch and nested objects where if the intermediate objects don't exist, it fails? Actually config.patch merges recursively, creating intermediate objects as needed. That should be fine.\n\nLet's try a simpler patch to test: maybe just set channels.discord.requireMention? But