{"type":"message","id":"db7c8163","parentId":"debbc2ba","timestamp":"2026-02-11T05:40:55.317Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":" unknown. Perhaps the channel ID format is wrong? In Discord, channel IDs are numeric strings (snowflakes). The ID from metadata is \"1471005448948813874\". That looks valid. But maybe the plugin expects the channel ID without the prefix? Or maybe the plugin doesn't have that channel in its allowlist because of groupPolicy? The config shows guilds.1444592258996244502.channels includes that channel ID (empty object). So it's allowed.\n\nMaybe the issue is that the bot needs to be in that guild and channel, and it's not? Or the Discord plugin may require the channel name rather than ID? The tool spec says `channel` is a string ID or name. I think ID should work.\n\nLet's try using the channel name? But I don't know the name exactly; it's \"#agent-ciel\", but that's the mention name. The actual channel name might be \"agent-ciel\". Could try \"agent-ciel\". But better to use ID.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I need to specify `accountId`? The config has accounts.default. Possibly the plugin expects the `accountId` to be \"default\". But the tool spec doesn't have that. Hmm.\n\nMaybe the search tool works differently: it might require `target` instead of `channel`. Let's re-read the tool spec. The message tool has actions: send, delete, edit, read, etc. The `search` action is listed under actions: \"search\". The parameters for `search` are:\n\n```\n\"properties\": {\n  \"before\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n  \"after\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n  \"fromMe\": {\"type\": \"boolean\"},\n  \"limit\": {\"type\": \"number\"},\n  \"query\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n  \"channel\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n  \"guildId\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n  \"accountId\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n  \"userId\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n  \"authorId\": {\"type\": \"string\"},\n  \"authorIds\": {\"type\": \"array\", \"items\": {\"type\": \"st