{"type":"message","id":"a144d5ed","parentId":"f6db77f2","timestamp":"2026-02-11T05:43:09.748Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":" is available. Good.\n\nNow I need to fetch messages from the channel. Discord's API: GET /channels/{channel.id}/messages?limit=100 (max). That returns up to 100 messages, ordered by timestamp descending (newest first). I need to delete all. I can fetch batches and delete each message, then use the `before` parameter to get older messages.\n\nBut I need to be mindful of rate limits: Discord allows 50 requests per second for message delete? Actually bulk delete can delete up to 100 messages at once for messages under 14 days, but that's separate. For individual deletions, rate limit is about 5-10 per second per channel? But we can just do one at a time with a short delay.\n\nBetter to use the bulk delete endpoint for messages younger than 14 days, but simpler to delete individually.\n\nWe'll fetch the first batch (limit=100). Then for each message ID, call DELETE /channels/{channel.id}/messages/{message.id}. Then use the last message's ID (the oldest) as `before` to fetch the next batch. Continue until we get less than limit.\n\nBut also we need to be careful: the bot token might be a user token with higher rate limits, but still.\n\nI'll write a shell script using curl and jq to parse. The gateway likely has jq? I can check. Let's see if jq is installed.\n</think>\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_cb78e3c76db4439b8afc3799","name":"exec","arguments":{"command":"which jq || echo \"no jq\""}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"stepfun-ai/step-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":117986,"output":327,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":118313,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770788579832}}
