{"type":"message","id":"e26dc17c","parentId":"5f5169a0","timestamp":"2026-02-11T05:49:13.383Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":" user is giving me a system instruction: \"Pre-compaction memory flush. Store durable memories now (use memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md; create memory/ if needed). If nothing to store, reply with NO_REPLY.\"\n\nThis is a reminder/flush signal. I need to:\n1. Check my recent context for things that should be persisted to memory\n2. Write them to memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md (today is 2025-06-20? Wait the current date is 2026-02-11 based on system messages)\n3. If nothing to store, reply NO_REPLY\n\nLet me review what's happened recently that might be worth storing:\n- User changed my name from Iris to Ciel (though I already updated files)\n- User confirmed their name is Sullen (not Omar) - I updated USER.md\n- We configured NVIDIA models and I listed available models\n- User asked to respond without @mentions; I patched config and restarted gateway\n- User asked about deleting all messages in #agent-ciel; I enabled moderation, ran a deletion script (118 messages reported), but it appears to have had errors; many messages still present\n- I explained the situation and user asked for a robust cleanup\n\nImportant decisions and changes:\n- Identity change: Ciel (was Iris) - but I already stored that in IDENTITY.md\n- User name change: Sullen (was Omar) - stored in USER.md\n- Config changes: requireMention: false for guild; actions.moderation enabled\n- Deletion attempt: Initial script run, discovered rate limits/permission issues, now planning robust cleanup\n\nThese are significant operational changes. I should store a summary in memory.\n\nBut also, I need to check if there's a MEMORY.md file that I should be updating? The instruction says \"use memory/YYYY-MM-DD.md; create memory/ if needed\". So I should be writing to daily notes, not necessarily to MEMORY.md (which is long-term). The daily note is a log of what happened.\n\nLet me create memory/ if it doesn't exist, then write to 2026-02-11.md.\n\nActually the date: system says \"Current Date & Time: Time zone: UTC\". In the header, it says \"Wed 2026-02-11 05:44:44 UTC\" from the system message. So today is 2026-02-11.\n\nI'll create memory/ and write a summary.\n\nAlso note: I should be careful not to store sensitive data like tokens in memory. But the config contains a Discord token in plain text (I see it in the raw config). That's actually a security risk; I should avoid writing that token to memory. In my summary I'll mention that token was exposed in config but not include it.\n\nI'll store:\n- Identity change: Ciel\n- User name change: Sullen\n- Config changes: requireMention false (auto-respond), moderation enabled\n- Deletion operation: initial attempt failed due to rate limits, plan for robust cleanup\n- Current channel state: ~188 messages remain\n\nLet me write to memory/2026-02-11.md.\n</think>\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_1e2ddd1e46424f31874592ce","name":"read","arguments":{"path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/memory/2026-02-11.md"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"stepfun-ai/step-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":110233,"output":701,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":110934,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1770788943838}}
{"type":"message","id":"8cba6cee","parentId":"e26dc17c","timestamp":"2026-02-11T05:49:13.398Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_1e2ddd1e46424f31874592ce","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# 2026-02-11\n\n## Discord Integration Setup\n\n- User provided Discord bot token: `MTQ3MDk5MDc0MzA5ODIzMzExMg.GS1nWd.02_4znxHWOy_xbn5yVqx9UScxQQNLyrsyr80Ys`\n- Enabled `@openclaw/discord` plugin via config patch\n- Configured token under `channels.discord.accounts.default.token`\n- Set `groupPolicy: \"allowlist\"` by default\n- Gateway restarted automatically\n\n## Next Steps (Pending)\n\n1. **Invite bot to Discord server** via OAuth2 URL generator (bot scope + appropriate permissions)\n2. **Allowlist channels**:\n   - Use `/pair` in desired channels for pairing approval\n   - OR manually configure guild/channel IDs under `channels.discord.guilds`\n3. Test bot responses\n\n## Technical Notes\n\n- Discord plugin is installed but was disabled; enabled via config\n- Token stored securely in config (will be redacted in logs)\n- Current configuration: `channels.discord.accounts.default` with token and `groupPolicy: \"allowlist\"`\n- No guild/channel allowlist configured yet, so bot won't respond until channels are added\n\n## User Preferences\n\n- User wants to use NVIDIA Integrate API with Kimi K2.5 (already configured)\n- Prefers direct, efficient communication\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1770788953388}}
