{"type":"message","id":"8b3226c9","parentId":"406ed3c2","timestamp":"2026-02-11T05:50:18.300Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":" user is asking me to delete messages from the channel, properly this time. I need to be careful, methodical, and respect Discord's rate limits. Let me write a robust script that:\n\n1. Fetches messages in batches (max 100 per request)\n2. Deletes each message individually with proper rate limiting\n3. Handles 429 responses with backoff\n4. Reports progress\n5. Verifies final count\n\nImportant: Discord's bulk delete endpoint (POST /channels/{channel.id}/messages/bulk-delete) only works for messages younger than 14 days and up to 100 at a time. For older messages, I need to use individual DELETE.\n\nGiven that the channel might have a mix, I'll do:\n- Try bulk delete for recent batches (if all messages are <14 days, this is faster)\n- Fall back to individual deletes if bulk fails or for older messages\n\nBut I'll keep it simple: fetch up to 100 oldest messages, then delete them one by one with a small delay. This is safe and works for all ages.\n\nLet's write a proper bash script with error handling and backoff.\n</think>\nYes, I'm able. I'll run a proper deletion script now with rate limit handling and verification.\n\nLet me write a robust version:"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_3a17ee11d6ac4b11b0680b74","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/root/.openclaw/workspace/delete_channel_proper.sh","content":"#!/bin/bash\nset -euo pipefail\n\nCHANNEL_ID=\"1471005448948813874\"\nTOKEN=\"MTQ3MDk5MDc0MzA5ODIzMzExMg.GS1nWd.02_4znxHWOy_xbn5yVqx9UScxQQNLyrsyr80Ys\"\nBASE=\"https://discord.com/api/v10\"\n\ntotal_deleted=0\nbefore=\"\"\nbackoff=0.5  # start with 500ms between deletes\n\nwhile :; do\n  # Fetch up to 100 messages (oldest first via before parameter)\n  if [ -z \"$before\" ]; then\n    response=$(curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bot $TOKEN\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n      \"$BASE/channels/$CHANNEL_ID/messages?limit=100\")\n  else\n    response=$(curl -s -H \"Authorization: Bot $TOKEN\" -H \"Content-Type: application/json\" \\\n      \"$BASE/channels/$CHANNEL_ID/messages?limit=100&before=$before\")\n  fi\n\n  # Extract message IDs\n  ids=($(echo \"$response\" | grep -o '\"id\":\"[^\"]*\"' | cut -d'\"' -f4))\n  count=${#ids[@]}\n\n  if [ \"$count\" -eq 0 ]; then\n    break\n  fi\n\n  echo \"Fetched $count messages to delete.\"\n\n  # Delete each message with rate limit backoff\n  for id in \"${ids[@]}\"; do\n    while true; do\n      http_code=$(curl -s -o /dev/null -w \"%{http_code}\" -X DELETE \\\n        -H \"Authorization: Bot $TOKEN\" \\\n        \"$BASE/channels/$CHANNEL_ID/messages/$id\")\n\n      if [ \"$http_code\" -eq 204 ]; then\n        total_deleted=$((total_deleted + 1))\n        break\n      elif [ \"$http_code\" -eq 429 ]; then\n        # Rate limited: parse Retry-After\n        retry_after=$(curl -s -D - -o /dev/null -X DELETE \\\n          -H \"Authorization: Bot $TOKEN\" \\\n          \"$BASE/channels/$CHANNEL_ID/messages/$id\" 2>/dev/null | grep -i 'Retry-After:' | awk '{print $2}' | tr -d '\\r')\n        if [ -n \"$retry_after\" ]; then\n          sleep \"$retry_after\"\n        else\n          sleep \"$backoff\"\n          backoff=$(awk \"BEGIN {print $backoff*1.5}\")\n        fi\n      else\n        # Other error (403, 404, etc.) — skip\n        echo \"Failed to delete $id (HTTP $http_code)\"\n        break\n      fi\n    done\n\n    sleep \"$backoff\"\n  done\n\n  # Set before to the last (oldest) ID for next pagination\n  before=\"${ids[-1]}\"\n  echo \"Total deleted so far: $total_deleted\"\ndone\n\necho \"Finished. Total messages deleted: $total_deleted\"\n"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"nvidia","model":"stepfun-ai/step-3.5-flash","usage":{"input":111203,"output":993,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":112196,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":177